WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.580
Technology has long been
an athlete's secret weapon.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.740
Searching for the
slightest competitive edge,

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.346
the best players across sports
are willing guinea pigs,

00:00:10.346 --> 00:00:13.010
and companies from the Fortune 500

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.503
to Silicon Valley startups know it.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.020
Tens of billions of dollars
are spent every year

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.140
on everything from the
newest shoe, to wearables,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.030
to Big Data-driven apps.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.100
But one of the biggest technologies

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.171 position:63%
to emerge in sports over the last decade

00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:31.110
is aimed at doing something
you don't traditionally see

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.853
in the classic training montage.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.740
Recovery technology
aims at helping athletes

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.600 position:58%
bounce back from the intense training

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.850 position:58%
and activity their bodies go through,

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.517
and make the most of those
high octane workouts.

00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:47.108
You do not get stronger that moment

00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:48.660
that you're lifting the barbell.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.110
You get stronger as your
body is making repairs,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.370
making recovery.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:57.810
Recovery is a win and how you
get fitter, faster, stronger.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.700 position:61%
Recovery technology includes everything

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.910
from massage guns and foam
rollers, to compression boots,

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.650
hyperbaric chambers, cryo
chambers, infrared saunas,

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.993
and even infrared pajamas.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.980
And athletes are partnering
to become investors

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.843
to take those products mainstream.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.510
When you look at tech
and sports right now,

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.730
it's completely innovating
the way training's going.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.980
Completely changing the
way recovery's going.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.560
I think sky's the limit
as far as where it can go.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.030
But while some of these products

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.840
can feel amazing, it can be
difficult to differentiate

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.634
between what really helps the body

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.920
and what just tricks the mind.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.950
So many of these things
end up not holding up.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.520
Every time you're chasing the
latest, greatest, newest tool,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.503
you're probably chasing a mirage.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.130 line:0%
So I'm a former D1 athlete myself,

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.869 line:0%
and nearly a decade ago, recovery looked

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:57.180
a lot different than it does now.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.340 position:59%
We made sure to recover from injuries.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.110
But for professional
athletes who have made it

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.224
their job to keep their bodies
operating at peak performance

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:08.130
even into their late
30s and sometimes 40s,

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.866
recovery is touted as one
of the most important tools

00:02:10.866 --> 00:02:14.906
to both prevent injury and
elongate their careers.

00:02:14.906 --> 00:02:16.680
I feel like it makes me feel better

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.020
and helps me recover faster.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.930 size:84% position:42% line:0%
This is an opportunity for
me to take care of my body.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.550 align:start position:0% line:0%
No pain, no gain.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.720
Recovery has also been

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.240 position:59%
a big source of business for athletes.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.560
While many athletes have appeared

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.810
in marketing for various products,

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.053
many are also making direct
investments into them as well.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.400
Including All-Pro running
back Christian McCaffrey,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.329
who not only uses products
created by company Hyperice,

00:02:41.329 --> 00:02:44.520
but he became an investor
in the business itself.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.100
When I first started talking
with everyone from Hyperice,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.510 size:78% position:39% line:0%
I had actually been a fan

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.760 line:0%
of the product myself for a long time.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.056
I think the biggest thing you get

00:02:52.056 --> 00:02:55.437
when you're dealing with recovery

00:02:55.437 --> 00:02:59.160
and the biggest thing that
athletes want is convenience.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.410 position:64%
Obviously, having suffered a few injuries

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.810
these last two years,
it has been very tough.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.290
And having products like
Hyperice have been huge for me

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:10.440
not just being able to
recover and come back quickly,

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.180
but also in training in general

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:15.450
and just staying at the top
of my game at all times.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.460 position:64%
Christian and other athletes have pointed

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.010
to the convenience
factor of these products.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.350
Giving them the ability to
work on their own bodies

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.090
outside of a training room.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.330
The amount of recovery that
you can do is limitless.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.030
You don't have to be in
the training room 24/7

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.110
to be able to recover.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.820 position:56%
You can kinda take ownership of that

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:33.900
at your house as well,

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.670
and not just sit there
in soreness and say,

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.320 position:58%
well, hopefully I feel good tomorrow.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.940
No, I can do something about it now

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.340
because I have something
in the palm of my hand.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.760
In 2020, the NFL made Hyperice

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.460
their official recovery
technology partner.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.070
Following investments from
athletes like Patrick Mahomes,

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.003 line:0%
J.J. Watt, Jarvis Landry, and McCaffrey,

00:03:53.003 --> 00:03:55.320 position:64%
players have been investing more and more

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.450
in other technologies as well.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.930
Some with clearly questionable
scientific support.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.970 line:0%
Tom Brady's sleep pajamas, for example,

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.511
rely on infrared
technology that they claim

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.130
helps promote better sleep.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.920
But not only is this
not approved by the FDA,

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.960 position:56%
the best studies for such technology

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.960
come from experiments with rats.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.360 position:64%
Still, recovery's importance for athletes

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.460 position:56%
has led it to become a big business.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.440
Hyperice is one of few major brands

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.410
that have taken recovery tools
used by professional trainers

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.800
and elite athletes and
marketed them for everyone.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.360
Hyperice has partnered with some

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.890
of the largest sports brands,

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:34.593
and is estimated to be
valued around $1 billion.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.930
One of their biggest competitors
in the space is Therabody.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.720
The company that created
the original Theragun,

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.693 align:start position:0% line:0%
which was made by this
guy, Jason Wersland.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.230 line:0%
2007, I was in a motorcycle accident.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.410
As a chiropractor, I knew
the things that I needed

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.200
and most of them were in
my office, in my practice.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.540
And I can't bend, bundle
'em up, and take 'em with me

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.520
so I just went to my garage
and I grabbed some tools

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.260
and brought 'em in and I started
messing around with them,

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.230
and I just made something and
I started using it on myself.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.660 position:59%
And when I tell people that it worked,

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.740 position:64%
meaning the pain stayed away for minutes,

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:11.760
20 minutes at a time.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.913
As long as I had it on my body,
I could tolerate the pain.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.270 position:59%
To say the least, that first prototype

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:20.790
was not a consumer facing device.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:24.000
But the principal idea, what's
known as percussive therapy,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.620
was there from the beginning.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.210
Percussive therapy as a concept

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.250
has been around for centuries.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.560
You can see it in a
Swedish massage technique

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.500
known as tapotement,
where hands and fingers

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.603 position:66%
are used to rhythmically drum on the body.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.440 position:63%
Here in the 1920s, you can see a similar

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.943
percussive therapy device.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:47.340
This stuff's been around
since the '40s and '50s.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:50.820
I mean, they used to take
like a blender sort of design

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.680 position:58%
that had an up and down motion to it,

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.110
and the doctors would
use that on a patient.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.370
Wersland would begin to tweak

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.100
his original design and
started to use his device

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.383 position:59%
on other patients facing similar pain.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.080
He contends that three factors

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.540 position:61%
in the design of the Theragun were key.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.640
The amplitude, or the
depth the massage ball

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.230
would move up and down.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.690
The frequency, the number
of times per second

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:16.200
it could move up and down,
and the torque or stall force.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.640
How much pressure you could apply

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.950
before the motor would stall?

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.800
The result, Therabody claims,
will increase blood flow

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.200 position:63%
and relieve tension and pain temporarily

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.670
in the treated area.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.010
Something that Wersland
initially found useful

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.633
in treating patients in pain.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.550
So how did it go from like
kind of working on injuries

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:38.760 position:59%
to I want to do this almost, you know,

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.110
every day to stay healthy?

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:40.943
Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:40.943 --> 00:06:43.070
So I would actually treat
athletes, celebrities,

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:46.590
and they would take my
product when I wasn't there

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.480
and they would take it
out on the gym floor.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.729
I would get so mad at them
and I asked one of them,

00:06:50.729 --> 00:06:52.140
what are you doing?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.910 position:59%
And he said, oh dude, this makes my...

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:54.900
I don't get sore.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.480
And so as he's telling
me this I'm thinking,

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.643 position:59%
holy crap, I didn't even realize that.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:01.410 align:start position:0% line:0%
Therabody would launch

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.470 size:88% position:44% line:0%
their first product in 2016,

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:06.240 align:start position:0% line:0%
but that was before
any scientific research

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.190 line:0%
could be done on the product.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:12.090
The Theragun got out way
before we could do studies.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.350
That was a tough thing for me

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.760 position:58%
because I was trying to hold it back,

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.798
waiting to get some validation.

00:07:16.798 --> 00:07:18.780 position:61%
Theragun would use athlete testimonials

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:21.900
to help sell those early
products to both other athletes,

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.720
and anyone else who
believed it could help.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:28.560
And made headlines when
during the 2017 NBA finals,

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.220
Kyrie Irving was spotted
using one on the sidelines.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.650 position:59%
But with attention came many companies

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.750
looking to compete in the space.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:38.850 position:63%
Today, a simple Amazon search can reveal

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.280 position:61%
the multitude of devices on the market.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.493
Some at a tenth of the
price of current Theraguns.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.020
In 2020, Theragun would
rebrand to Therabody,

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:55.230
and the company would expand
into other recovery products.

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.730
Continuing to take equipment

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.710
that originated in training rooms,

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.590
and bringing them to
the general population.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.923
It's also opening locations
like this, called Reset.

00:08:04.923 --> 00:08:09.540 position:59%
The idea for Reset came from us seeing

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.580
these things behind doors,

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.210
and not allowing the general
population to experience it.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:17.100
We couldn't like ignore it.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:22.100
This room is our Theragun
and stretch room.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:26.020
So if you were here today,
I would take these two

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.403
and I would treat your body-

00:08:28.403 --> 00:08:29.640
At the same time.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.863 position:56%
Yes, it's called a double gun sweep.

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.680
The location allows you to choose

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.840
from a menu of sorts for recovery.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.300
Allowing you to experience
both Therabody products

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.580 position:59%
used by their staff, but also products

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.850
you typically wouldn't see
outside of elite training rooms.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:48.000
Things like a red light
table, hyperbaric chambers,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.533
and a cryo chamber.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.980
I'm gonna open this just to
give you the effect of it.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:58.560
Oh, lordy, lordy.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:08:59.910
Yeah.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:02.130 position:63%
It's set for two minutes and 30 seconds.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.750
It's not that long.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:04.950
Are you gonna try this?

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:07.140
Now, I'm not one to back
down from a challenge.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:09.780
So I put on some protective
equipment for my hands and feet,

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:10.980
and stood inside the chamber

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:14.565
at negative 141 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:09:14.565 --> 00:09:16.980
While the Jonas Brothers
blasted in my headphones

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.690
to help keep my mind from freezing

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.990
for the two and a half minutes,
I couldn't help but wonder.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.610
Is all of this technology aimed

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.880 position:56%
at recovering our bodies worth this?

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.430
Little frost on your eyelashes.

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.590 position:63%
Athletes should be prioritizing recovery

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.350
in the same way that
they prioritize training.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.330
It's that important.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.070 size:88% position:44% line:0%
This is Christie Aschwanden.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:40.342 size:81% position:41% line:0%
A journalist, and author
of the book, "Good To Go,"

00:09:40.342 --> 00:09:42.813 align:start position:0% line:0%
where she wrote about
the science of recovery.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:47.250
I read hundreds probably
close to a thousand

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.720
scientific research articles

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:49.920
while I was working on the book,

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.050 position:58%
looking at all sorts of these things.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.210
And I can just say having done that

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:57.090
and having interviewed
hundreds of researchers,

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:58.530
that there's not a lot of evidence

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.780
that this stuff does much.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.910 position:64%
Professional sports teams spend millions,

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.740 position:56%
if not billions of dollars each year

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.900
in various sports science fields.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:10.200
Players themselves also invest
heavily on their own health.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.007 position:56%
LeBron James reportedly spends about

00:10:12.007 --> 00:10:15.783 position:56%
$1.5 million on his body every year.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.910
I want this stuff to work.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.850
I'll tell you what, you know,
I was willing to try anything

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.110
while I was working on this book.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:25.200
I tried almost all of these
major recovery techniques

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.707 position:64%
that are being marketed now for recovery,

00:10:27.707 --> 00:10:29.790 position:58%
but what I found is that most of them

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:33.093
if they made a difference, the
difference was very marginal.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:37.890
Including, unfortunately
for me, cryotherapy.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:39.930 position:63%
In her book, Christie points to research

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.900
that couldn't establish any
evidence of recovery benefits

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:45.390
in whole body cryotherapy.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.640
The FDA would also put
out a consumer warning

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.920
about the lack of evidence
for the treatment,

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.273
and warned of potential risks.

00:10:52.273 --> 00:10:54.243
You wanna see it?

00:10:54.243 --> 00:10:55.680
Are you sure you wanna see it?

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.630
Frostbite is reportedly to blame

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.190
for sidelining Antonio Brown.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.050 position:61%
He reportedly went to France last month

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.790
to undergo cryotherapy.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.160
The source says he didn't
wear the proper footwear,

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:08.430
and as a result, his
feet were frostbitten.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.410 position:66%
Despite this, elite teams around the world

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:12.450
continue to use cryotherapy.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.090 position:66%
In 2021, the Dallas Cowboys even announced

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:17.610
an official cryo partner.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.740
There's really good
evidence for some things

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.540
that really do help recovery.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:24.180
It's sleep, it's stress reduction.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:25.710
These are things that, you know,

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:29.040
are very hard to commercialize,
very hard to monetize.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.800
What we're seeing now
though, is sports leagues

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.650
you know, everyone wants to
keep up with everyone else.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:38.580
And when you see your competition
using this new device,

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.440 position:61%
you think, well, we have to do that too

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:41.940
because what if it works?

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:45.540
And so it's not even about
the science necessarily,

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.510
it's about the culture of this
is what everyone's doing now

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.130
so we'd better be doing it.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:52.320
When it comes to devices
like massage guns,

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.158
the amount of research is
still relatively small.

00:11:55.158 --> 00:11:58.620
Some studies of recovery
technology products have concluded

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:00.840
they show beneficial effects.

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:03.630
But while the industry
has touted such findings,

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.880 position:61%
the studies generally use small samples

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:09.270
and often themselves call for
the need for more research.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.283
Some are also not peer reviewed.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.520
The quality of the science

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.860
in a lot of fields of sports
science is pretty low,

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.840 position:56%
and this is not to slam researchers,

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.240
it's that these studies
are really hard to conduct.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.400
It's difficult particularly
if you're looking

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:24.840
at elite athletes.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.850
I mean, you tell me how
you're gonna do a study

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.380
where you take elite athletes

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.118 position:56%
and you ask them to change something

00:12:30.118 --> 00:12:31.980
so that you can study it.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.060
They're not gonna do that.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.865 position:58%
Most of these studies are very small,

00:12:34.865 --> 00:12:38.070
and so the results that they
get aren't very reliable.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.810 position:56%
There's a lot of uncertainty in them

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:42.480
so I think we just have
to be very careful.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.530
Now this is changing.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.555 position:64%
I think there's a growing recognition now

00:12:45.555 --> 00:12:47.970 position:64%
that there needs to be more rigor applied

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.590
to these sorts of studies.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.540
It's not an easy nut to crack.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.580 position:56%
It's hard to get bigger sample sizes

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.880
for some of these studies.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.490
Conclusive, scientific
research takes time.

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:01.650 position:66%
And with new devices coming out every year

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:03.990
and eager athletes willing to try,

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.840
it may be a while before we
could definitively understand

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.840
what products are actually
doing to your body.

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.088
But it's important to know

00:13:11.088 --> 00:13:13.980
that while there may not be
conclusive, scientific evidence

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:17.040
of physiological gains
from recovery devices,

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.980
that doesn't necessarily
mean they aren't effective,

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.470 position:58%
especially when it comes to the mind.

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.930
I don't wanna be too
dismissive of this stuff.

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:27.420
You know, some of these
massage tools feel really good,

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:28.530
and that's worth something.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.400
It really is.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.387
And if you feel better
using these massage tools,

00:13:32.387 --> 00:13:34.080
I say go for it.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.480
The placebo effect is
often sort of dismissed

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.550
as something that's no good,

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.860
but I think that it's something
that we can, in some cases,

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.743
really, you know, harness for good.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:45.990
I wanted to come to a place

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.450
where these types of
devices were being used.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.127 position:58%
Here at the University of Pittsburgh,

00:13:50.127 --> 00:13:52.140
athletic trainers work to take care

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.480 position:58%
of the student athletes holistically.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.520 position:63%
You'll see many of the same devices here

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.170
that are used by the staff.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.330
But as they explain,
they're working not just

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:03.093
to treat students' bodies,
but their minds as well.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:07.470 position:61%
There's more than one thing that we do.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:09.420 size:75% position:38% line:0%
Not a lot, but there are
some things that we do

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:12.150 align:start position:0% line:0%
that are for the placebo
effect to make someone think

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.170 align:start position:0% line:0%
we're doing something.

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.720
You know, there's something
to be said for rest.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.030
This is Jennifer Brown,
the senior associate

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.950 position:58%
athletic director for sports medicine

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:21.450
at the University of Pittsburgh.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:24.030 position:64%
And she oversees all areas of performance

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:26.310
including nutrition,
strength and conditioning,

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:28.260
as well as mental health.

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.660
Rest and recovery is so important,

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:32.441
and the more we do this,
the more we realize

00:14:32.441 --> 00:14:34.560
the importance of those.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.700
Athletes are competitive.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.560
They wanna know what
they do to get better.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.720
Some of them thinks
it's go, go, go, go, go.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:42.210
Well, we know if you keep
going and keep going,

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.100
no matter who you are,
at some point in time,

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:45.270
something's gonna break.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:47.100 position:66%
And do you think that's where some of that

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:50.820
recovery placebo tech can come in

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.920
where you're trying to
get them to understand

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:54.480
that they need to rest?

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.760 position:59%
So it's like let's bring this thing in

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:59.700
that makes them think that
that's what's happening.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:00.900
Like, they're still doing something

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:03.330
but it's actually just helping
them rest a little bit?

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:04.470
Absolutely.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:07.830
There's a lot of times where
we're like, hey, do this.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.160
It's for nothing else than
to have them sit down.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.500
They don't like the
concept of doing nothing

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:14.940
and completely resting.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.367
And so what can we do
that seems like something

00:15:17.367 --> 00:15:19.440 position:58%
and that is helping them in some way,

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.540
but isn't too much or too taxing.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.545
I would say the vast
majority of these products

00:15:23.545 --> 00:15:26.940
that target recovery are
really just giving athletes

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.220
something to do while
they wait for their bodies

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:31.260
to recover on their own naturally.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:34.173
You know that happens whether
you use these devices or not.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:36.540
But as Jennifer explains,

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.450
that time isn't just useful
for their body health.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.620
The mental side of the game

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.240 position:56%
is something companies like Hyperice

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.440
are already interested in.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:47.340
In 2021, Hyperice bought the
mental wellness company, Core.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.990
LeBron has also gotten in the game

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:51.150 position:64%
and partnered with Calm to create content

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.400
meant to promote mental fitness.

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.230
You know, when I was
growing up or, you know,

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.100
some of our coaches,

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.200
we talked about, mental
health had a stigma to it.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:59.323
You had a mental illness.

00:15:59.323 --> 00:16:01.260
Do we really talk about that?

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.460
Well, that has changed.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.310
We certainly have people that
are mental health therapists,

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.440
and social workers,
counselors, psychiatrists,

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.810 position:66%
psychologists, that that's their training.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:12.480
But, you know, as athletic
trainers or, you know,

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:15.060
even coaches or our, you
know, academic advisors,

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:17.010
we're all talking to students

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:18.700
and it's just, you
know, caring about them,

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:21.840
making sure we are
genuine, making sure we're,

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:24.120 position:56%
you know, asking people how are you?

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:24.990
How are you?

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:27.299
And listening, not just
passing in the hallway,

00:16:27.299 --> 00:16:30.510
but like actually
listening to what they say.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.830
Not judging them.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:35.970
Everybody's perception is
different, but to each individual,

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.943
what they perceive is
what matters to them.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.210 position:61%
What might work for one player mentally

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:43.920
could be different for another,

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:46.920
and the same is true when it
comes to recovery technology.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.920 position:66%
It's all about making sure they feel good.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:51.780
While our most popular
games have been played

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.610
nearly the same way for decades,

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:57.030
everyone from coaches
to players, to owners,

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.220
to your average enthusiast
is always looking

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.020
for the next competitive edge.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.790
And technology will always be there

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.973
to provide at least the chance
for the next big advantage.

